From d48cfba4d28b2636566a105b529da528393d1fd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Karsten Sperling <ksperling@apple.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 17:50:57 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] RADIUS server: Pass consistent tls_flags

Ensure the tls_flags passed to tls_init() and tls_global_set_params()
match, so the overall behavior is consistent between TLS backends (Only
WolfSSL actually honors flags passed to tls_init()).

Signed-off-by: Karsten Sperling <ksperling@apple.com>
---
 hostapd/radius.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hostapd/radius.c b/hostapd/radius.c
index 0b4f76ee2..97dce56ae 100644
--- a/hostapd/radius.c
+++ b/hostapd/radius.c
@@ -564,6 +564,11 @@ static int radius_setup(struct radius_state *s, struct radius_config *c)
 		.cb_ctx = s,
 	};
 
+	/* Most backends ignore tls_config.tls_flags. Pass identical flags
+	 * via tls_connection_params so the behavior is the same either way. */
+	c->tls.flags |= conf.tls_flags;
+	conf.tls_flags = c->tls.flags;
+
 	eap->eap_server = 1;
 	eap->max_auth_rounds = 100;
 	eap->max_auth_rounds_short = 50;
-- 
